{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793824001,"nonce":"cqmUla5pkYg35YekHsfdelbtLNE=","title":"OSR: reuse return facts across regions of one module snapshot","message":"Allocation and nonnull return inference currently scan the immutable module again for every outlined OSR region. Temporary local diagnostics on crypto_pyaes show 8-9 invocations scanning a 355-function module per process. Each scan pair takes about 0.5-0.8 ms (nonnull roughly 0.33-0.51 ms, allocation roughly 0.19-0.27 ms), about 4-5 ms combined. This is diagnostic CPU work, not an isolated wall-time attribution; the repeated crypto slowdown in f1273ca remains to be measured against the candidate.\n\nCache both analyses by immutable Arc module identity, with bounded storage, weak module ownership and one initialization shared by concurrent requests. Mutation through Arc::make_mut must invalidate the identity; no reuse solely by module name or HirId. Do not retain unloaded module bodies or hold the Cranelift lock during analysis. Preserve interpreter-first startup and compute facts only when OSR requires them.\n\nCandidate tests cover concurrent sharing, invalidation after mutation, dead-module release and bounded entries. Frozen-binary NUC comparison and the full pinned TS corpus are required before landing. Local diagnostics and validation live at /private/tmp/zyntax-osr-next/.","files":null}]}